    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0111" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg37"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burnley</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 31, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of the 6th instant, requesting that the Secretary of the
                    Navy may take into serious consideration the proofs which you offer of the
                    neutrality of the Night Hawk, <pb facs="0112" n="38" xml:id="pg38"/> and, in
                    reply, to inform you that I have invited his attention to a copy of your note
                    and the original register of the vessel, with the request that he may return the
                    register after having considered its contents.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the renewed assurance of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
